 it in torchtext.Field. then the export generated a useless\ninput to trace the model, so i switched that out for the first example\nin the dataset. present situation is: `RuntimeError: Tried to trace\n<__torch__.brevitas.core.quant.RescalingIntQuant object at 0x55b84e4f5130>\nbut it is not part of the active trace. Modules that are called during\na trace must be registered as submodules of the thing being traced.`\nthere seems to be some support online:\n- is it possible the input is supposed to be quantized?\n- should try pytorch-nightly\n- why are we using brevitas when real full-fledged libs exist (caffe\nseems to be one of them)\n- i don't know how quantization really works, or what's really going\nwrong, or if brevitas would be able to trace modules that were only\nincluded in later versions. so, not sure where to go from here", "created_at": "2020-06-17T14:23:59Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8dbc1a4abab033a1f6a5f246c3aa053773155bac", "message": "included onnx export module\n\ni full-on stole the export module from a feature branch in brevitas, about 100 commits behind\nthis means that that version does not include conv1d, so i'm using \"globally\" installed brevitas\n+ locally shoved module for onnx export. now have to pick a specific size, pad the whole\ndataset, pass the size to the finn export and it should be working.\nhopefully the Conv1D won't be SO different (unlikely) that the export func does not know how\nto deal with it\nnot sure how the padding thing is done. i guess the BucketIterator already knows how to do it,\nbut setting a really high batch size seems very stupid. also, now i get why the example network\nin brevitas was fixed-size :/", "created_at": "2020-06-11T13:08:02Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "70156550815739ef9ac27659a04236025e18865b", "message": "removed useless code, included suggestions for next time\n\nwasted a few hours trying to find brevitas onnx. turns out, it's not\nmentioned in the master branch or in documentation. it was, in fact,\nin a feature branch! also, it seems to require a fixed input size.\nnext time will have to check", "created_at": "2020-06-09T21:07:14Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3af6576204854912b369f2e5a1cf808de0e054ab", "message": "gave ONNX a try... brevitas did not like that", "created_at": "2020-06-09T14:05:43Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1668960a2a5d87aecb592e34bc48658661e9fc96", "message": "lowered epoch max", "created_at": "2020-05-29T13:08:44Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "94000fda490fd9064f2a217b74b2188a209545a8", "message": "using quantized model... might actually be working", "created_at": "2020-05-29T13:02:37Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2b00229743447595c71390f48dc6006afa631afe", "message": "small bugfix", "created_at": "2020-05-28T14:44:15Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "554844ea937637c6b89c3088368d3440d459dd9c", "message": "made directory relative", "created_at": "2020-05-28T14:24:09Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f058069cd361266fa6bdf4690da96c17ed656e6c", "message": "included new dataset. change 67 for different file", "created_at": "2020-05-28T14:23:35Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "9eab52540c35723a1017d5d437483aab03c5de90", "message": "changed model dirs, included simple roadmap", "created_at": "2020-05-27T11:27:51Z", "repo": "learNN", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c3d362df8ef87cb3938d866bc72